    "order": 4,
    "title": "Interpolator selected by minimizing mirror potential in underdetermined linear regression",
    "content": "For underdetermined linear regression problems $f(x)=\\tilde f(Zx-Y)$ with $n>d$, if $f$ is quasi-convex, $\\nabla f$ is locally Lipschitz, and $\\operatorname{argmin}_{x\\in\\mathbb{R}^n} f(x)$ is non-empty, then gradient flow on the overparameterized variables $(m,w)$ (with $x=m\\odot w$) converges to a limit $x^*$ that solves\n      $$\n      x^* \\;=\\; \\operatorname{argmin}_{Zx=Y} R(x),\n      $$\n      i.e., among all interpolators $x$ satisfying the data constraints $Zx=Y$, gradient flow selects the one minimizing the Bregman potential $R$ induced by the $m\\odot w$ parameterization.",
