    "title": "Convergence and linear rate for time-dependent potential (PILoT) under PL",
    "content": "Let $\\alpha_t\\ge 0$ satisfy $\\int_0^\\infty \\alpha_s ds<\\infty$, and assume $f$ is quasi-convex or satisfies the PL inequality with constant $\\lambda>0$. Consider the time-dependent Bregman potential $R_{a_t}$ given by $R_{a_t}(x)=\\frac{1}{2}\\sum_{i=1}^n\\left(x_i\\operatorname{arcsinh}\\!\\left(\\frac{x_i}{a_{t,i}}\\right)-\\sqrt{x_i^2+a_{t,i}^2}-x_i\\log\\!\\left(\\frac{u_{0,i}}{v_{0,i}}\\right)\\right)$ with $a_{t,i}=2u_{0,i}v_{0,i}\\exp\\!\\left(-2\\int_0^t\\alpha_s ds\\right)$, $u_{0,i}=\\frac{m_{0,i}+w_{0,i}}{\\sqrt{2}}$, $v_{0,i}=\\frac{m_{0,i}-w_{0,i}}{\\sqrt{2}}$. Then the time-dependent mirror flow $d\\nabla R_{a_t}(x_t)=-\\nabla f(x_t)dt$ converges to a critical point $x^*$; if $f$ is convex or satisfies PL then $x^*$ is an interpolating minimizer of $f$. In the PL case the loss satisfies the finite-time bound\n      $$\n      f(x_t)-f(x^*) \\le B\\exp\\!\\big(-\\lambda a_\\infty t\\big),\n      $$\n      where $a_\\infty=\\lim_{t\\to\\infty}a_t$ and\n      $$\n      B=(f(x_0)-f(x^*))\\exp\\!\\Big(C||x^*||_{L_2}\\!\\int_0^\\infty\\alpha_s ds\\Big),\n      $$\n      with $C$ a constant depending on the smoothness of $f$.",
